# The oracle's Maven output. `target` is in the repo-root .gitignore for
# upstream's modules, but that file is upstream's and is not edited (ADR-0001),
# so crucible/ covers its own.
/oracle-java/target/

# Compiled Go commands. `go build ./tools/x` writes the binary into the module
# root named after its package. Named explicitly rather than by a broad
# pattern, so a future Go source file cannot be silently ignored.
#
# This list goes stale whenever a tool is added, so it is not the guard. The
# guard is the CI step that rejects any tracked binary under crucible/,
# whatever it is called.
/apiscan
/carddump
/covergate
/crucible
/docgate
/enginelint
/genapitype
/genparams
/javacycles
/vocabscan

# Coverage profile, written by the test step and read by covergate.
/cover.out
